@page "/page-recipes"

<CatHead Title="Page recipes" Tier="@CatHead.Tier2">
    Whole pages, composed from the classes on the other pages: the list a record is found in, the
    record itself, and the settings behind it. Each one is the content of the shell's
    <code>.page</code> &mdash; take the frame from <a href="/frame">Shell</a>.
</CatHead>

<div class="callout callout--info">
    <i class="ri-information-line"></i>
    <div class="callout-body">
        <span class="callout-title">These are compositions, not new classes</span>
        Copy a recipe whole and change its content. Every class in it has a page of its own that says
        what it is for; a part a recipe leaves out is still on that page.
    </div>
</div>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.PageRecipes.ListPage" Title="A list page" Demo="ex-demo--block">
    <p>
        A page head whose actions fold into a menu on a narrow screen, keeping the primary one; a
        toolbar with the filters on the leading side and the count on the trailing one; a card holding
        a sortable table that stacks into cards on a phone; and the pager under it. When no row
        matches, the table keeps its head and shows one <code>.tr-empty</code> row, as on
        <a href="/table">Tables</a> &mdash; the page does not swap to an empty state for a filter
        that found nothing.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.PageRecipes.DetailPage" Title="A detail page" Demo="ex-demo--block">
    <p>
        The trail back to the list, a page head naming the record, and <code>.sedna-split</code>: the
        record's fields in a card of <code>.kv</code> rows &mdash; <code>.kv--text</code> for a value
        that is prose &mdash; beside an aside holding its history. The aside drops under the card when
        the split runs out of room.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.PageRecipes.SettingsPage" Title="A settings page" Demo="ex-demo--block">
    <p>
        One <code>.form-section</code> per subject, each with a line saying what it is for, and one
        <code>.form-actions</code> row for the whole form. A switch applies a choice; Save applies
        the fields &mdash; if a switch should wait for Save too, make it a checkbox.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.PageRecipes.PageFeedback" Title="Page feedback" Demo="ex-demo--block">
    <p>
        At the foot of a page, after its content: one question and two answers. <strong>Yes</strong>
        records the answer and replaces the row with the thanks; <strong>No</strong> and
        &ldquo;Report a problem&rdquo; replace it with a short form of two open questions, and Send
        replaces the form with the thanks. All three are one region whose content the app swaps, so
        focus and the reader's place stay where they were; send the page's address with the answer.
        Ask for nothing personal, and say so above the fields.
    </p>
</CatExample>
